{
  "_note": "Crafting (by hand and at the Crafting Bench) and the Cutter, read by both editions. Things are named by their keys (see blockKey in index.html / DataKeys.cs).",
  "_notes": {
    "RECIPES": "every crafting recipe, in the order the recipe lists show them (the ones you can make right now go first): out = what it makes, n = how many; needs = [[thing, how many], ...] (all used up); at = hand (anywhere: the inventory, E) or bench (only at a Crafting Bench, which also makes the hand ones); axe = also needs an axe in your hotbar, tool = also needs that tool in your hotbar (neither is used up); colour = only listed while you carry at least one of its ingredients; tall = only while tall worlds are on (the deep layers' Stone)",
    "CUTTER": "the Cutter's shapes, in the order of its buttons: mode = the shape (pieces, or the shape's name in keys like slab:stone), label = its button, uses = blocks it takes, makes = how many you get (pieces: always 8, a block's 8 spots)"
  },
